# MASTER CORE FRAMEWORK CONVENTIONS & ARCHITECTURE

## 1. NESTJS BACKEND CONVENTIONS

- Force strict compliance with the Repository Design Pattern wrapper for Prisma/TypeORM layer queries.
- Expose endpoints uniformly across Websockets, GraphQL resolvers, and REST endpoints using structured data interceptors.
- Forbid any inline SQL mutations; route all graph states through targeted service modules.

## 2. NEXT.JS & REACT CONVENTIONS

- Implement React Server Components (RSC) by default for data fetching; limit use of 'use client' strictly to interactive UI nodes.
- Manage websocket stream contexts natively using decoupled React context providers.

## 3. TAILWIND V4 & SHADCN UI CONVENTIONS

- Strictly utilize Tailwind v4 native CSS-based configuration entry points (`@theme`) instead of legacy JavaScript configurations.
- Enforce semantic variable mapping for dark/light state variables.
- Customize shadcn primitives inline inside the components library directory tree; forbid modifying the underlying Radix base values directly.
